# restart, persisted choices, preserved account data, guarded workers/auth callbacks.
#
# 157 rebase: android-components was reformatted (ktfmt) and FxA moved on. The
# sync token cache (SyncAuthInfoCache, maybeUpdateSyncAuthInfoCache,
# AccessTokenUnexpectedlyWithoutKey) and AccountScopeAccessor are gone upstream,
# so their admission checks went with them; authenticationSideEffects() now only
# resolves the device id, which is fenced instead. New 157 entry points gated:
# handleWebChannelPasswordChange(), encounteredAuthError(), and Send-to-Device's
# sign-in redirect (HomeActivity.handleSendToDevicesActionIntent opens Settings).
# SyncConfig/SyncEngine moved to concept.sync; sync worker runs on
# GlobalAccountManager.syncIoDispatcher and rustSyncManager. Tests: the three
# token/endpoint/missing-key race tests are replaced by one device-id race test;
# AccountServicesWorkerTest reads sync state through SharedPrefsSyncStateStorage;
# HomeActivityAccountSettingsTest stubs components for 157's Glean debug-tag hook.
# Integration: regenerated on top of the 157 no-glean, whose deletion of the
# Glean debug-tag lines sat in this patch's HomeActivity hunk context (fuzz 2).
#
# 158 rebase (2026-10-04, pre-rebase against Firefox 158.0b3): same guards,
# three moved:
#   * FxaAccountManager.start(): 158 calls syncManager?.initialize() before
#     processQueue(Event.Account.Start). The disabled-services guard is put
#     first, so with account services off start() returns before the sync
#     manager is initialised as well (157 had nothing before processQueue).
#   * WorkManagerSyncDispatcher's immediate-sync method now logs the custom
#     engine subset first; the AccountServices.isEnabled guard stays the first
#     statement.
#   * HomeActivity.onCreate(): the two savedInstanceState reads that became
#     accountSafeSavedInstanceState sit behind reformatted context.
# The other hunks needed fuzz 1-2 on 158 and are regenerated at fuzz 0.
